.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-wallets-tokens - Choose which tokens (and chains) a wallet accepts


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 wallets tokens [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage a wallet's token holdings — the (chain, token) pairs it accepts.

.PP
They are what 'payment-methods' offers buyers and what payment creation checks:
a wallet with no active holding cannot be paid. Every holding survives being
disabled, so re-enabling one keeps its history.

.PP
A wallet with active holdings always has exactly ONE default, the method a buyer
is offered first. The first holding you add takes it; to move it, run
\&'wallets tokens add' on the new one with --default. The gateway refuses to
disable the default (422 default_payment_method) — move it first.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tokens


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 wallets tokens add 0xABCD… --chain-id 84532 --token USDC --default
  rail0 wallets tokens disable 0xABCD… USDC --chain-id 84532
  rail0 wallets tokens enable 0xABCD… USDC --chain-id 84532
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-wallets(1)\fP, \fBrail0-wallets-tokens-add(1)\fP, \fBrail0-wallets-tokens-disable(1)\fP, \fBrail0-wallets-tokens-enable(1)\fP
